{:repo "octave-commons/muse", :lesson "A policy system may legitimately contain several different algebras: severity decisions can join, fulfillments can accumulate, precedence rules can choose the first decisive result, and process transformations can compose separately. Do not collapse these into one generic meaning of composition. Reduce semantic decisions without erasing causal witnesses; provenance can obey different laws from the decision it explains.", :research "docs/research/2026-08-07-policy-algebra-pass-8.md", :status :orientation}
